:Region a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Region" ;
    rdfs:comment "A top-level geographic grouping of nations (TPC-H regions: AFRICA, AMERICA, ASIA, EUROPE, MIDDLE EAST). The root of the geography hierarchy — a Nation belongs to exactly one Region, and customers/suppliers roll up to a region through their nation." .

:Nation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Nation" ;
    rdfs:comment "A country (TPC-H has 25). The middle level of the geography hierarchy: a Nation belongs to one Region (see edges) and is the nation of customers and suppliers. The grain at which most geography filtering happens before rolling up to Region." .

:PartSupp a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "PartSupp" ;
    rdfs:comment "The supply of a Part by a Supplier — a reified many-to-many relationship with its own attributes (available quantity, supply cost). Identified by the composite key (ps_partkey, ps_suppkey). It is an entity, not an edge, precisely because it CARRIES data: an edge cannot hold availqty/supplycost." .

:Supplier a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Supplier" ;
    rdfs:comment "A party that supplies parts. Identified by s_suppkey and located in one Nation (see edges). The supply side — which supplier provides a part, at what cost, is captured by PartSupp." .

:Customer a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Customer" ;
    rdfs:comment "A party that places orders. Identified by c_custkey, located in one Nation (see edges), and classified by a market segment. The demand side — orders and revenue attribute to a customer." .

:Orders a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Orders" ;
    rdfs:comment "The header of a customer order: who placed it (one Customer), when, its total price and status. The parent of one or more LineItems. Modelled as an entity (a header record); the fulfilment lifecycle lives on its LineItems, which is where shipping actually happens." .

:Part a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Part" ;
    rdfs:comment "A catalogue item that can be ordered. Identified by p_partkey, classified by brand and type. Sold through one or more suppliers (see PartSupp) and bought on order lines." .

:LineItem a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "LineItem" ;
    rdfs:comment "A single line of an order — one part, supplied by one supplier, in some quantity at some price. The central fact of TPC-H (composite key order + line number). It is an EVENT: it is shipped, received, and possibly returned, moving through a fulfilment lifecycle read from its ship/receipt dates and status flags. Revenue is computed from its extended price and discount." .

